  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an array AAA of integers of length NNN. Find the sum of difference between maximum and minimum elements of all sub-arrays. Formally, find the value of the following expression :\n∑i=1N∑j=iNmax(Ai,Ai+1...Aj)−min(Ai,Ai+1...Aj)\\sum\\limits_{i=1}^{N}\\sum\\limits_{j=i}^{N} max(A_i, A_{i + 1} . . . A_j) - min(A_i, A_{i + 1} . . . A_j)i=1∑N​j=i∑N​max(Ai​,Ai+1​...Aj​)−min(Ai​,Ai+1​...Aj​)\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, number of testcases. Then the testcases follow.\nFirst line of each testcase contains a single integer NNN.\nSecond line of each testcase contains of NNN integers : A1,A2...ANA_1, A_2 . . . A_NA1​,A2​...AN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase, output a single integer equal to the value of given expression.",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= T <= 100",
      "1 <= N <= 100000",
      "1 <= Ai <= 100000",
      "The sum of N over all test cases does not exceed 2*10^6."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line contains an integer T, the number of test cases. For each test case, the first line contains an integer N, the length of the array. The second line contains N space‑separated integers A1, A2, …, AN.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case output a single line containing the sum of (maximum – minimum) over all sub‑arrays of the given array.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3\n1 4 9\n3\n5 5 5",
        "output": "16\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest-case 1:\nConsider all the sub-arrays of given array\n\n[1]\n[1, 4]\n[1, 4, 9]\n[4]\n[4, 9]\n[9]\n\nThe desired value = (1−1)+(4−1)+(9−1)+(4−4)+(9−4)+(9−9)=16(1 - 1) + (4 - 1) + (9 - 1) + (4 - 4) + (9 - 4) + (9 - 9) = 16(1−1)+(4−1)+(9−1)+(4−4)+(9−4)+(9−9)=16"
      }
    ]
  },
