  "solution": {
    "approach": "For each element we count how many sub‑arrays have it as the maximum and how many have it as the minimum. Using a monotonic stack we can find, for every position i, the distance to the previous greater element (strict) and the next greater‑or‑equal element. The product of these two distances gives the number of sub‑arrays where A[i] is the maximum. The same is done for minima using previous smaller (strict) and next smaller‑or‑equal elements. The answer is Σ A[i] * (cntMax[i] – cntMin[i]). All operations are O(N) per test case.",
